# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Portfolio 2.0 — dineshrevunuru.com
#  Lorem, the voice agent at /lorem, is the only thing here that needs config.
#
#    cp .env.example .env.local        .env.local is gitignored. Never commit keys.
#    npm run check:keys                verifies keys without printing them
#
#  NAMING, so a line's job is obvious at a glance:
#    LOREM_*          a choice this app makes    (which model, which provider)
#    <VENDOR>_*       a vendor's own credential  (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, …)
#    NEXT_PUBLIC_*    reaches the browser        (never put a secret here)
#
#  Lorem makes three model calls per turn: a BRAIN that composes the answer,
#  a VOICE OUT that speaks it, a VOICE IN that hears the visitor. The sections
#  below are in that order. Everything after them is optional.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ══ 1 · BRAIN ════════════════════════════════════════════════ required ══════
# Composes every turn. Without this Lorem loads, greets from pre-rendered audio,
# then fails on the first real question.

# Which provider. "anthropic" or "openrouter". Lorem runs on OPENROUTER —
# that is where google/gemini-3.7-flash lives. Anthropic stays wired as the
# fallback for when OpenRouter's balance hits zero, which has happened.
# Unset picks Anthropic, unless only an OpenRouter key is present.
#
# ⚠ NOT interchangeable at the wire level. app/api/lorem/route.ts keeps a
# separate request/response path for each: system prompt is a top-level field
# vs a first message, tools are {name, input_schema} vs {type:"function",
# function:{...parameters}}, forced-tool syntax differs, and returned arguments
# arrive parsed vs as a JSON string. Switching this var is safe. Hand-editing
# one path is not.
LOREM_BRAIN=anthropic

# https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# Set a monthly spend cap in the console: /lorem is public and unauthenticated.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

#   REQUIRED — this is the brain Lorem actually runs on. Steps:
#     1. Get it at https://openrouter.ai/keys
#     2. Set a CREDIT LIMIT on the key — /lorem is public and unauthenticated,
#        so that limit is the only real ceiling on spend.
#     3. Change LOREM_BRAIN above to:  openrouter
#     4. npm run check:keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# The model. Unset takes the provider's default:
#   openrouter  → google/gemini-3.7-flash   what Lorem runs on. 1.05M context,
#                                           $0.375/M in, $1.875/M out.
#   anthropic   → claude-sonnet-5           the fallback path only.
#
# ⚠ Any replacement MUST list "tools" and "tool_choice" in supported_parameters
# at https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models. The guardrail reads a forced tool
# call and never free text, so a model without them cannot drive this route.
#
# ⚠ AND its schema subset matters. Google's function declarations accept
# `oneOf` and then IGNORE it — the request succeeds and the model answers with
# empty blocks, so the visual track goes dark while speech sounds fine and
# nothing errors. protocol.ts derives a flattened schema for this path
# (RESPOND_TOOL_FLAT) to work around it. A new provider needs the same check:
# ask a question that should draw a metrics block and confirm one arrives.
LOREM_MODEL=

# Reasoning effort. "low" on purpose: short conversational composition with
# someone waiting, not multi-step reasoning.
LOREM_EFFORT=low

# Extended thinking. "adaptive" costs ~0.55s over three turns and buys the
# judgement this surface sells — which blocks to show, how to split say from
# show. The numbers guardrail catches invented figures; nothing catches a
# careless block choice. "disabled" trades it back.
LOREM_THINKING=adaptive


# ══ 2 · VOICE OUT ═══════════════════════════════════════════ recommended ════
# How Lorem speaks. Falls back to browser speech when the key is missing, so a
# misconfiguration makes Lorem sound worse rather than go silent.

# "elevenlabs" · "openai" · "browser"
#
# NOT offered: OpenAI Realtime speech-to-speech. S2S audio can't be made
# deterministic, so the spoken track would be model-paraphrased — and the whole
# guardrail here is that a number cannot be invented. With S2S the screen stays
# safe and the voice doesn't. The cascade keeps both honest.
LOREM_TTS=elevenlabs

# https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Lorem's established voice, shared with aria-portfolio and saathi. Keep it
# unless deliberately re-casting: one person sounding like two is a tell.
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=X03mvPuTfprif8QBAVeJ

# Live turns. eleven_v3 is the expressive model and the ONLY one that accepts
# audio tags — which is how Lorem carries warmth without claiming a feeling.
#
# ⚠ Affordable only because the audio path streams end to end. Measured on a
# 44-word answer: ~510ms to first audio streaming, ~6s buffered. TWO things
# hold that up, and breaking either silently restores the six-second wait:
#   · /api/voice must call the /stream endpoint
#   · useSpeech must feed MediaSource, not await res.blob()
# Safari has no MediaSource for audio/mpeg and pays full generation time.
#
# eleven_flash_v2_5 is the fast alternative (~135ms) and loses the tags.
# eleven_turbo_v2_5 is DEPRECATED — ElevenLabs marks it outclassed by Flash.
ELEVENLABS_MODEL=eleven_v3

# Fixed lines (the greeting), rendered once by scripts/prerender-voice.mjs.
# Latency is paid at build time, so this stays on the best model regardless of
# what the live model is set to.
ELEVENLABS_PRERENDER_MODEL=eleven_v3


# ══ 3 · VOICE IN ════════════════════════════════════════════ recommended ════
# How Lorem hears. Scribe also makes voice input work in Firefox and Safari,
# where the browser recognizer doesn't exist.

# "elevenlabs" (Scribe) or "browser" (Web Speech: free, weaker).
# With Scribe on, the browser recognizer still runs where available purely to
# drive the live caption — Scribe's transcript is the one the brain receives.
LOREM_STT=elevenlabs

# scribe_v2 only. scribe_v1 is accepted but marked Deprecated; not a fallback
# worth having. Uses ELEVENLABS_API_KEY above.
ELEVENLABS_STT_MODEL=scribe_v2


# ══ 4 · SITE ════════════════════════════════════════════════ production ═════
# Both are NEXT_PUBLIC_ and therefore visible in page source. Neither is secret.

# ⬇ LEAVE BLANK HERE. This is not a missing value — set it ONLY in Vercel's
#   Production scope. Unset resolves: VERCEL_ENV=production → the real domain,
#   else VERCEL_URL → this deployment, else localhost. That ordering is what
#   makes previews fail CLOSED, refusing crawlers and analytics. Filling it in
#   locally would make your machine claim to be production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Microsoft Clarity project id — session replay, heatmaps, rage clicks.
# https://clarity.microsoft.com → Settings → Setup
# Production scope only; Clarity.tsx additionally refuses any host that isn't
# dineshrevunuru.com, so previews can't pollute the heatmaps.
# Blank disables tracking entirely.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID=


# ══ 5 · OPTIONAL ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Conversation logging → the training loop. Both from the Supabase project:
# Settings → API. The SERVICE ROLE key, not anon — the table's RLS has no
# policies, so anon sees nothing (deliberate). Unset = logging off, Lorem
# unaffected. Run scripts/lorem-turns.sql in the SQL editor once first.
# Pull what lands:  npm run pull:conversations
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Only when LOREM_TTS=openai. https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_TTS_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini-tts
# alloy · echo · fable · onyx · nova · shimmer
OPENAI_TTS_VOICE=alloy

# Points the brain call at a mock upstream. Local testing only.
# LOREM_API_URL=

# Gym only (test/gym/). Unset uses the built-in default, which stays on
# claude-sonnet-5 DELIBERATELY now that the brain is Gemini:
#   · a judge that shares the brain's model grades its own output
#   · every baseline score so far was Sonnet-judged, so moving the judge and
#     the brain at once makes a score change impossible to attribute
# The measuring instrument does not move at the same time as the thing measured.
# GYM_VISITOR_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# GYM_JUDGE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5


# ── Legacy ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BOO_MODEL, BOO_EFFORT, BOO_THINKING, BOO_VOICE_PROVIDER, BOO_STT_PROVIDER and
# BOO_API_URL are the pre-rename names, from when this agent was called Boo.
# config.ts still reads them as a fallback so a deploy that still has them set
# does not silently lose its voice provider. Delete that fallback in config.ts
# once Vercel holds only LOREM_* names.
